<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GENTYRE HALF YEAR PROFITS SKID LOWER.</title>
<headline>GENTYRE HALF YEAR PROFITS SKID LOWER.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	 40	  vs    130</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    -	  vs     48</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   6.87	  vs  21.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.56	  vs  27.93</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.68	  vs   6.41</p>
<p>    Interest received     1.47	  vs   1.52</p>
<p>    Operating profit	8.10	  vs  26.41</p>
<p>    Turnover		332.54	  vs 311.30</p>
<p>Full name: Gentyre Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The tyre maker said it was deferring consideration of</p>
<p>an interim dividend until after the March 12 budget.</p>
<p>Gentyre said it had been hit by intense local market</p>
<p>competition and weak European markets, which impacted on</p>
<p>exports. Industrial action at the Port Elizabeth plant in</p>
<p>October and November had severely affected production.</p>
<p>But chief executive Johan Bester said the outlook for the</p>
<p>remainder of the financial year was better.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
